We have read our bubble sort.

5
00:00:10,520 --> 00:00:13,200
After that, we have read the selection sort.

6
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:15,720
After that, we have read the insertion sort.

7
00:00:15,720 --> 00:00:18,800
After that, we have read our counting sort.

8
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:21,760
Apart from this, we have read an inbuilt sort as well.

9
00:00:21,760 --> 00:00:24,680
That is, if I have an array that I want to sort,

10
00:00:24,680 --> 00:00:25,680
then what can I do?

11
00:00:25,680 --> 00:00:29,000
I can use a simple function for that.

12
00:00:29,200 --> 00:00:32,480
All these sorting comes into our basic sorting.

13
00:00:32,480 --> 00:00:35,440
Inbuilt sort is always optimized sorting.

14
00:00:35,440 --> 00:00:38,240
But today, we will read about another different sorting technique

15
00:00:38,240 --> 00:00:39,360
