So, this can be asked in interviews,

23
00:00:56,840 --> 00:00:59,280
or in your college exams.

24
00:00:59,280 --> 00:01:02,520
And you can directly ask questions to implement it

25
00:01:02,520 --> 00:01:03,840
by some companies.

26
00:01:03,840 --> 00:01:05,960
That is why Merge Sort is very important.

27
00:01:05,960 --> 00:01:07,960
Now, the time complexity of Merge Sort

28
00:01:07,960 --> 00:01:09,600
comes as much as an inbuilt sort,

29
00:01:09,600 --> 00:01:11,760
that is, it comes equal to n log n.

30
00:01:11,760 --> 00:01:13,680
When we read the time complexity chapter,

31
00:01:13,680 --> 00:01:15,000
then we will discuss in detail

32
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:18,920
why the time complexity of Merge Sort comes to n log n.

33
00:01:18,920 --> 00:01:21,040
So, we will not take any tension about it now.

34
00:01:21,040 --> 00:01:23,280
We already know that sorting means

35
00:01:23,280 --> 00:01:27,320
arranging elements in a particular order.

36
00:01:27,320 --> 00:01:30,920
That particular order can be an ascending order,

37
00:01:30,920 --> 00:01:33,280
or a descending order.

38
00:01:33,280 --> 00:01:34,920
In fact, there are more orders.

39
00:01:34,920 --> 00:01:38,720
But here, we will assume that in ascending-descending order,

40
00:01:38,720 --> 00:01:40,600
we sort our elements.

41
00:01:40,600 --> 00:01:42,240
So, what will be useful for us?

42
00:01:42,240 --> 00:01:44,840
Today, we are taking an example of ascending.

43
00:01:44,840 --> 00:01:46,680
We have given an unsorted array

44
00:01:46,680 --> 00:01:49,840
in which some random elements are stored.

45
00:01:49,840 --> 00:01:53,240
That is, 6, 3, 9, 5, 2, 8.

46
00:01:53,280 --> 00:01:55,360
We have to convert this unsorted array

47
00:01:55,360 --> 00:01:57,840
into this sorted array.

48
00:01:57,840 --> 00:02:00,440
And all the elements in the sorted array

49
00:02:00,440 --> 00:02:03,160
are arranged in our ascending order.

50
00:02:03,160 --> 00:02:04,520
Now, there is an ascending order here,

51
00:02:04,520 --> 00:02:06,400
but we will change the condition a little bit.

52
00:02:06,400 --> 00:02:09,200
So, we can write the same algorithm for descending.

53
00:02:09,200 --> 00:02:12,360
To solve our array, we will use Merge Sort.

54
00:02:12,360 --> 00:02:14,280
Now, there are three steps in Merge Sort

55
00:02:14,280 --> 00:02:16,000
that we have to follow.

56
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:19,840
So, the first step in the approach

57
00:02:19,840 --> 00:02:21,880
is called to divide.

58
00:02:21,880 --> 00:02:25,920
That is, we have to divide the pieces of our problem

59
00:02:25,920 --> 00:02:27,120
into small problems.

60
00:02:27,120 --> 00:02:31,040
For that, we will take out the mid of our array.

61
00:02:31,040 --> 00:02:33,080
For example, if I have this array,

62
00:02:33,080 --> 00:02:34,360
what will be its mid?

63
00:02:34,360 --> 00:02:38,000
I can either take this index or this index.

64
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:40,600
So, if my array has my starting index 0

65
00:02:40,600 --> 00:02:43,240
and my ending index is its length minus 1,

66
00:02:43,240 --> 00:02:46,440
which is 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5.

67
00:02:46,440 --> 00:02:48,040
So, I have the ending index 5.

68
00:02:48,040 --> 00:02:51,200
So, for this array, I will have the middle index.

69
00:02:51,200 --> 00:02:53,240
I can select any of these two.

70
00:02:53,240 --> 00:02:56,400
Let's assume that the middle index I selected for my array

71
00:02:56,400 --> 00:02:57,880
is this index.

72
00:02:57,880 --> 00:03:01,760
That is, here, I want to partition my array.

73
00:03:01,760 --> 00:03:04,480
So, my problem will be divided into two parts.

74
00:03:04,480 --> 00:03:07,160
Which part will be the first part of my left part?

75
00:03:07,160 --> 00:03:10,480
The left part will say that I don't want to sort the big array.

76
00:03:10,480 --> 00:03:13,440
Now, I only want to sort 6, 3 and 9.

77
00:03:13,440 --> 00:03:15,560
And the second part will be my right part.

78
00:03:15,560 --> 00:03:18,800
The right part will say that I don't want to sort the big array.

79
00:03:18,800 --> 00:03:20,920
I only want to sort 5, 2 and 8.

80
00:03:20,920 --> 00:03:23,000
I want to sort this small array.

81
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:26,560
So, I have divided my big problem into two parts.

82
00:03:26,560 --> 00:03:27,720
How did I divide it?

83
00:03:27,720 --> 00:03:30,640
First, I have found out the middle of my array.

84
00:03:30,640 --> 00:03:33,160
After that, I have partitioned it from here.

85
00:03:33,160 --> 00:03:36,520
I have partitioned it or divided it into two parts.

86
00:03:36,520 --> 00:03:40,080
Now, I will divide this array into smaller and smaller parts

87
00:03:40,080 --> 00:03:41,360
and how long I will divide it

88
00:03:41,360 --> 00:03:43,360
until I get my smallest problem

89
00:03:43,360 --> 00:03:46,320
or the easiest to solve problem.

90
00:03:46,360 --> 00:03:51,040
For example, if I have a problem to sort these three numbers of the array

91
00:03:51,040 --> 00:03:53,320
then what will I do? I will find out the middle of it.

92
00:03:53,320 --> 00:03:55,080
What will the middle of it have?

93
00:03:55,080 --> 00:03:58,440
In this, I can say that the starting index is 0

94
00:03:58,440 --> 00:04:01,680
and my ending index is going to be 2.

95
00:04:01,680 --> 00:04:05,160
So, the middle element of it will be coming here.

96
00:04:05,160 --> 00:04:07,800
So, this problem will also be divided into two parts.

97
00:04:07,800 --> 00:04:09,440
One will be my left part.

98
00:04:09,440 --> 00:04:12,680
The left part will say that you don't want to solve the big array.

99
00:04:12,680 --> 00:04:15,160
You only want to solve the big array of 6 and 3.

100
00:04:15,160 --> 00:04:17,200
The first part will be my right side part.

101
00:04:17,200 --> 00:04:20,200
The right side part will say that we don't want to solve the big array.

102
00:04:20,200 --> 00:04:22,720
We only want to solve the 9th array.

103
00:04:22,720 --> 00:04:25,520
Similarly, I can also partition here.

104
00:04:25,520 --> 00:04:28,880
For partitioning here, the middle will come here.

105
00:04:28,880 --> 00:04:30,400
If the middle comes, then one will come.

106
00:04:30,400 --> 00:04:34,160
The left part will say that you don't want to solve the big problem.

107
00:04:34,160 --> 00:04:36,720
I have to divide the problem into five and two

108
00:04:36,720 --> 00:04:40,120
and divide it to the right side to this single 8.

109
00:04:40,120 --> 00:04:44,080
Now, can I say that I cannot divide this problem any more?

110
00:04:44,080 --> 00:04:46,760
Because if there is a single element in an array,

111
00:04:46,760 --> 00:04:48,560
then doesn't it already have a sorted array?

112
00:04:48,560 --> 00:04:51,320
So, it doesn't need to sort it.

113
00:04:51,320 --> 00:04:54,920
So, this part here is already sorted.

114
00:04:54,920 --> 00:04:58,640
This part here is already sorted.

115
00:04:58,640 --> 00:05:01,000
I still have to solve this small problem.

116
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:02,760
This is my problem already solved.

117
00:05:02,760 --> 00:05:04,480
So, what I will do for this small problem?

118
00:05:04,480 --> 00:05:05,800
I will make it smaller.

119
00:05:05,800 --> 00:05:09,080
I will keep making it smaller until it is already solved.

120
00:05:09,080 --> 00:05:12,080
So, I will take out its middle again

121
00:05:12,080 --> 00:05:15,600
and partition it and divide it to a smaller problem.

122
00:05:15,600 --> 00:05:19,400
The smaller problem will be that you solve only the 6th array.

123
00:05:19,400 --> 00:05:22,640
Now, you just sort the 3rd array.

124
00:05:22,640 --> 00:05:24,520
I can do the same thing here.

125
00:05:24,520 --> 00:05:26,440
I will partition it in the middle here

126
00:05:26,440 --> 00:05:30,360
and say that we have to solve only the left problem.

127
00:05:30,360 --> 00:05:32,200
That is, we have to sort the 5th one

128
00:05:32,200 --> 00:05:35,480
and in the right one, I have to sort the 2nd one.

129
00:05:35,480 --> 00:05:37,880
Now, do I need to divide these problems as well?

130
00:05:37,880 --> 00:05:38,840
No, why?

131
00:05:38,840 --> 00:05:42,080
Because now, I have a small problem in the last one.

132
00:05:42,080 --> 00:05:44,240
I have single elements in it.

133
00:05:44,240 --> 00:05:45,520
And what are single elements?

134
00:05:45,520 --> 00:05:46,960
They are already sorted.

135
00:05:46,960 --> 00:05:50,760
So, this array here will be sorted.

136
00:05:50,760 --> 00:05:53,040
This will also be sorted.

137
00:05:53,040 --> 00:05:55,080
This will also be sorted.

138
00:05:55,080 --> 00:05:57,120
This will also be sorted.

139
00:05:57,120 --> 00:05:58,240
So, what did I do?

140
00:05:58,240 --> 00:06:02,480
I took out my big problem and divided it into small parts.

141
00:06:02,480 --> 00:06:07,400
Until then, I don't have the smallest part.

142
00:06:07,400 --> 00:06:10,240
And as soon as I got this smallest part,

143
00:06:10,240 --> 00:06:12,240
the smallest problem that was divided,

144
00:06:12,240 --> 00:06:13,720
it is already sorted.

145
00:06:13,720 --> 00:06:15,320
So, here I did my first step.

146
00:06:15,320 --> 00:06:19,840
The first step was to divide my problem into smaller subparts.

147
00:06:19,840 --> 00:06:22,160
Now, another thing to note here is that

148
00:06:22,160 --> 00:06:26,440
every time I have to solve the part of my array,

149
00:06:26,440 --> 00:06:28,960
if I know the starting index of that part

150
00:06:28,960 --> 00:06:30,360
and know the ending index,

151
00:06:30,360 --> 00:06:33,800
as I knew at first, my array's starting index is 0

152
00:06:33,800 --> 00:06:35,520
and my ending index is 5.

153
00:06:35,520 --> 00:06:37,000
Can I take out the middle element from the starting index

154
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:40,720
and the ending index as I did in my binary search?

155
00:06:40,720 --> 00:06:43,040
How do we take out the middle element from the starting and the ending?

156
00:06:43,040 --> 00:06:43,960
There are two ways.

157
00:06:43,960 --> 00:06:47,920
Either I write the starting index plus the ending index divided by 2.

158
00:06:47,920 --> 00:06:49,800
Or I write the second way.

159
00:06:49,800 --> 00:06:53,880
The starting index plus the ending index minus the starting index

160
00:06:53,880 --> 00:06:55,440
divided by 2.

161
00:06:55,440 --> 00:06:58,240
I will return the correct answer in both the ways.

162
00:06:58,240 --> 00:07:01,280
But I will not use this method.

163
00:07:01,280 --> 00:07:02,440
We can also use this method.

164
00:07:02,440 --> 00:07:03,960
The answer will be correct.

165
00:07:03,960 --> 00:07:07,720
But the problem will be solved when we have a very big array.

166
00:07:07,720 --> 00:07:09,600
What happens in a very big array?

167
00:07:09,600 --> 00:07:13,160
Sometimes, if I talk about the starting index and the ending index,

168
00:07:13,160 --> 00:07:15,640
then these two can be big integer values.

169
00:07:15,640 --> 00:07:19,800
And the value of these two can sometimes be bigger than the size of the total integer.

170
00:07:19,800 --> 00:07:23,840
So, the size of the integer overflows with that value.

171
00:07:23,840 --> 00:07:26,600
In that case, we either have to take out the big data types

172
00:07:26,600 --> 00:07:28,760
or we can use this formula.

173
00:07:28,760 --> 00:07:32,320
I am talking about the basic math here.

174
00:07:33,280 --> 00:07:36,360
I can also convert this formula and bring it here.

175
00:07:36,360 --> 00:07:37,160
How?

176
00:07:37,160 --> 00:07:40,160
If I divide the starting index, then this will be

177
00:07:40,160 --> 00:07:43,280
the ending index divided by 2 minus the starting index divided by 2.

178
00:07:43,280 --> 00:07:45,480
The value of this will be the ending index divided by 2.

179
00:07:45,480 --> 00:07:47,920
And if I add this with this, then this will be

180
00:07:47,920 --> 00:07:50,280
plus the starting index divided by 2.

181
00:07:50,280 --> 00:07:53,040
This is equal to the ending index plus the starting index divided by 2.

182
00:07:53,040 --> 00:07:55,640
So, this formula and this formula are the same thing.

183
00:07:55,640 --> 00:07:58,840
In this thing, I do not have two big, big sizes of integers

184
00:07:58,840 --> 00:08:02,040
and they are not overflowing with my data types.

185
00:08:02,040 --> 00:08:04,480
So, the clarity of two or three things came to me in this step.

186
00:08:04,480 --> 00:08:07,760
First of all, I have to divide my problem

187
00:08:07,760 --> 00:08:11,320
until I get sorted in my small problem.

188
00:08:11,320 --> 00:08:13,320
And the smallest problem that has been sorted,

189
00:08:13,320 --> 00:08:16,200
I can say that this is going to be my base case.

190
00:08:16,200 --> 00:08:19,360
The base case for which I already know the solution.

191
00:08:19,360 --> 00:08:21,840
I know that if I get a single size area,

192
00:08:21,840 --> 00:08:23,400
then what will be the solution for that?

193
00:08:23,400 --> 00:08:25,480
In the solution, I do not have to do anything.

194
00:08:25,480 --> 00:08:27,280
I already have sorted it.

195
00:08:27,280 --> 00:08:30,040
Second thing, I analyzed that if I know the starting index

196
00:08:30,040 --> 00:08:31,960
and the ending index of any area,

197
00:08:31,960 --> 00:08:35,200
then I can get the middle of this formula.

198
00:08:35,200 --> 00:08:37,360
I have covered this step one.

199
00:08:37,360 --> 00:08:39,200
Now, let's talk about step two.

200
00:08:39,200 --> 00:08:43,200
Step two tells me that as soon as I took out my problem,

201
00:08:43,200 --> 00:08:45,120
my big problem,

202
00:08:45,120 --> 00:08:48,080
I took out the left part of it by dividing it from the middle

203
00:08:48,080 --> 00:08:50,040
and I took out the right part of it.

204
00:08:50,040 --> 00:08:50,920
So, what do I do?

205
00:08:50,920 --> 00:08:54,920
Recursively, now I call this left part and sort it

206
00:08:54,920 --> 00:08:57,920
and I call this right part and sort it.

207
00:08:57,920 --> 00:08:59,880
So, what do I have to do in step two?

208
00:08:59,880 --> 00:09:02,720
For my merge sort,

209
00:09:02,720 --> 00:09:06,360
first, I have to get the left part sorted.

210
00:09:06,360 --> 00:09:07,520
Then what do I have to do?

211
00:09:07,520 --> 00:09:11,000
I have to apply the merge sort to the right part.

212
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:12,840
If I take an example of this,

213
00:09:12,840 --> 00:09:16,600
then if I have an array of 639528,

214
00:09:16,600 --> 00:09:18,280
then what do I have to do?

215
00:09:18,280 --> 00:09:21,400
First of all, I have to partition it from the middle.

216
00:09:21,400 --> 00:09:22,960
After partitioning from the middle,

217
00:09:22,960 --> 00:09:27,800
I will get some left part which will be 639

218
00:09:27,800 --> 00:09:32,280
and I will get some right part which will be 528.

219
00:09:32,280 --> 00:09:33,200
Now, what do I have to do?

220
00:09:33,200 --> 00:09:37,320
I have to convert it into a sorted way by merging it.

221
00:09:37,320 --> 00:09:39,480
That is, I have to convert it into 369,

222
00:09:39,480 --> 00:09:42,000
and I have to convert it into 258.

223
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:46,120
I don't have the logic to see how I will convert it into a merge sort.

224
00:09:46,120 --> 00:09:50,760
But I have to get this part sorted and get this part sorted.

225
00:09:50,760 --> 00:09:52,240
Do you know how I will get that sorted?

226
00:09:52,240 --> 00:09:53,600
I will get it from the recursion.

227
00:09:53,600 --> 00:09:55,560
I will divide it into small parts.

228
00:09:55,560 --> 00:09:57,320
This will be the way of my recursion.

229
00:09:57,320 --> 00:10:00,760
But yes, I will get it sorted in some way.

230
00:10:00,760 --> 00:10:02,880
And then I will apply my step 3.

231
00:10:02,880 --> 00:10:05,240
Step 3 is to merge.

232
00:10:05,240 --> 00:10:09,640
That is, if my left part is sorted and the right part is sorted,

233
00:10:09,640 --> 00:10:14,120
then I will make a big solution by combining the solution of left and right.

234
00:10:14,120 --> 00:10:17,840
Let's see how I will make a big solution.

235
00:10:17,840 --> 00:10:18,880
This was my array.

236
00:10:18,880 --> 00:10:20,920
I divided it into two parts.

237
00:10:20,920 --> 00:10:22,400
Step 1 was to divide.

238
00:10:22,400 --> 00:10:23,480
What did I do in step 2?

239
00:10:23,480 --> 00:10:28,320
In step 2, I converted it into 369 by sorting the left part.

240
00:10:28,320 --> 00:10:31,800
And I converted my right part into 258 by sorting the right part.

241
00:10:31,800 --> 00:10:35,960
Now my job is to merge the third step.

242
00:10:35,960 --> 00:10:37,800
What will I do to merge?

243
00:10:37,800 --> 00:10:41,840
To merge, I will make a temporary array.

244
00:10:41,840 --> 00:10:44,280
I can name this temporary array.

245
00:10:44,280 --> 00:10:46,720
I will make the temporary array of the same size,

246
00:10:46,720 --> 00:10:51,080
in which all the elements on the left and all the elements on the right come.

247
00:10:51,080 --> 00:10:52,280
What will be its size?

248
00:10:52,280 --> 00:10:56,600
Its size will be left elements plus right elements.

249
00:10:56,600 --> 00:11:01,120
The total number of left elements plus right elements will be the total combined size.

250
00:11:01,120 --> 00:11:04,200
That will be the size of this temporary array.

251
00:11:04,200 --> 00:11:10,000
Now in the temporary array, I can say that I should have the space of 6 elements.

252
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:13,120
Now I know that my left part is sorted.

253
00:11:13,120 --> 00:11:15,800
And my right part is also sorted.

254
00:11:15,800 --> 00:11:20,160
Now I have to merge this sorted part and make a big sorted array.

255
00:11:20,160 --> 00:11:21,520
What will I do for that?

